//? Title: Jarvis march: choose one supporting edge at a time
//? Subtitle: Exact signs, actual candidate histories and output-sensitive wrapping
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Gift wrapping scans the cloud once for each hull vertex. We start with an actual
candidate replacement, retain the original twenty-point example, and distinguish
wrapping work from sorting overhead. Exact orientation signs and a same-ray
ordering rule handle finite binary64 coordinates without rounded distance
overflow. Owned native histories expose the producing decisions. Degenerate
controls and deterministic hull-size families make the limits visible.
)

\toc

> Watch one candidate change

In the five-point square below, the first candidate is the upper-left corner.
The centre temporarily replaces it, before the lower-right corner wins. An
intermediate incumbent need not be a hull vertex. The diagram shows the operands
and outcome of the first actual test; its arrows describe evaluation flow, not
geometric edges. Sorted indices and original input rows are different
identities.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/jarvis_candidate.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/jarvis_analysis.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <limits>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <cmath>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto t =
        dm::geometry::jarvis_march_trace({{0, 0}, {4, 0}, {4, 4}, {0, 4}, {2, 2}});
    std::print("| sorted index | original row | x | y |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.sorted.size(); ++i) {
        const auto &p = t.sorted[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, p.input_index, p.point.x,
                   p.point.y);
    }
    std::print("\n| first edge test | incumbent before | examined | exact sign | incumbent after |\n| ---: " "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.events.size(); ++i) {
        const auto &e = t.events[i];
        if (e.step == 0 && e.action == dm::geometry::JarvisAction::Test)
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, e.before, e.examined,
                       e.turn, e.after);
    }
    std::print("\nThe complete run returns {} vertices after {} orientation tests and {} actual events.\n",
               t.analysis.hull.size(), t.analysis.work.orientation_tests,
               t.events.size());
    dm::geometry::jarvis_candidate_diagram(t).save_svg("build/jarvis_candidate.svg");
}
```
